      "title_align": "left",
      "section": "Confidence of the model",
      "order": 3,
      "alignment": "left",
      "vertical_alignment": "top",
      "body": "How far to trust the predicted structure of the demo protein. The error matrix (synthetic: low inside each confident segment, high between segments and around the low-confidence ends) beside the structure and its written sequence; a synthetic S4PRED-style prediction against the call from the structure's own geometry, with two deliberate disagreements; the backbone torsions computed in the browser; and the sequence track. Brush the matrix diagonal, the ribbon or the track, or click a point or a letter, to select that range in every tile; hover marks it.\n",
      "surface": "none",
      "accent": null,
      "logo": null,
      "logo_dark": null,
      "wf_tag": "python/advanced_viz_demo"
    },
